/-! # `#machine_no_ports_kids` on `mid2` AS AN ENTRY: a domain-polymorphic parent of a child with a one-output gate call (G1, round par/a-22)

`mid2` (`Tests/Compiler/ShippingDesignSVTest.lean` 24–32):

    @[hardware_module]
    def mid2 {dom : DomainConfig} (en : Signal dom Bool) : CntOut dom :=
      circuit do
        let r ← Signal.reg 0#8
        let rs := (r : Signal dom (BitVec 8))
        let k := midH en            -- CntOut: n : BitVec 8, hit : Bool
        r <~ Signal.mux k.hit (rs + k.n) rs
        return ({ n := rs, hit := k.hit } : CntOut dom)

with `midH → rcH` (`Tests/Compiler/ShippingMachineDepthHTest.lean` 19–32:
`midH` a register machine with ONE one-output call of the gate child `rcH`).

By READING: `mid2 → midH → rcH` is `grandH → midH → rcH` — a parent WITH a
register under the general closing whose one callee is a register machine
with one-output calls of ONE gate child, depth 1: the scope
`#machine_no_ports_kids` states (`Tools/ShippingNoPortsKidsCommand.lean`,
`scopeK` 76–127). `grandH` at depth 1 is BUILT by hand and REBUILT by that
command (`docs/parallel/verification-a14b.md`); `mixD1` is GENERATED by it.
`mid2` was never an ENTRY of any design-level generator: it is `topD2`'s
child (`topD2.machine_design_noPortsNR2`, `…NR3` are about `topD2`'s run;
they give nothing about a run of the compiler ON `mid2`). No new theorem is
written in this file: BUILT commands are run on one more declaration.

What is NEW against `grandH` / `mixD1` (both over `defaultDomain`, both with
a `Signal` result): the ENTRY is domain-polymorphic and its result is a
STRUCTURE (`CntOut`), one field (`hit`) a field of the call's result passed
through. The same two differences were new for `mid` against `parent` /
`chained` / `two` under `#machine_no_ports` (BUILT, `NoPortsMidTest`); under
`#machine_no_ports_kids` they were never run.

## What the steps build on (READ in the sources named)

* `mid2.closes_deep` EXISTS in the imports: `#machine_closes_deep topD2`
  (`Tests/Compiler/ShippingCallsCloseDeepTest.lean` 33) adds `c.closes_deep`
  for every machine descendant with calls; "with TWO premises, the
  reflections of `midH` and `rcH`" (`Tests/Compiler/NoPortsTopD2Test.lean`
  49, BUILT). `noPortsKids` takes `f.closes_deep` when it exists
  (`Tools/ShippingNoPortsKidsCommand.lean` 667–670).
* `midH.closes_deep` (left by `#machine_closes_deep grandH`), `midH.oneout_*`
  and `midH.machine_portsRawH` (`OneOutMidHTest`, BUILT), `rcH.gate_full` /
  `gate_kidK` / `gateValue`: what `scopeK` asks of a one-output callee
  (lines 119–124); all were in `grandH`'s BUILT environment, which is this
  file's (`NoPortsGrandHBTest`).
* `mid2.machine_ships_hierNR1` does NOT exist: `#machine_design_svNR topD2 2`
  composes `mid2` as a child at depth 1 and adds no shipping theorem of
  `mid2`'s own entry. It is generated HERE, first.

