## What is NOT known before the build

1. whether `#machine_design_svNR mid2 1` goes through (a polymorphic parent
   with a structure result over a child with children: `mid` is the built
   polymorphic case, but its child is a leaf);
2. the decided data conditions of the generated `mid2.machine_kidsK1`,
   `_runFactsK1`, `_outsGK1`, `_maskedGK1`, `_designPK1` (a failed `decide`
   is reported by the command with the theorem's name);
3. the binder order `closedTerm` expects of the open form (the closing
   binder before the gate grandchild's trailing reflection) for a
   polymorphic entry;
4. the number of proposition binders of the closed form: 4 is ASSERTED
   below (the run and one reflection each of `mid2`, `midH`, `rcH`), by
   analogy with `mixD1`'s asserted 5; it is LOGGED before the assertion.

## SCOPE (binding for any report)

ONE declaration, `mid2`, AS AN ENTRY: a parent WITH a register under the
general closing, one callee (`midH`: a register machine with a one-output
call of the gate child `rcH`), depth 1. Data conditions decided per
declaration; compiler guards with fallback; `DesignSV` of the module list —
